The scheme worked by taking the first letter of each word in a designated audit passage and reading those letters in order. Spaces and punctuation in the resulting hidden text could then be restored to make words. The passage generally started after “Audit:” and stopped at “[End audit]” or before an explicitly separate constraint note. The surrounding text discussed assignments, shifts, adjacency, ordering, and verification, making the message look like ordinary puzzle work.

